Z||000023||Archie||09-04-2001||11:38 PM||||Hugh, I agree with you, but you might as well give it up. You can talk until you are blue in the face and there will still be a bunch of punks who will refuse to act human. You see dis-respect everyday in life and in this Forum. If the parents of these children didn't teach them to show respect for others, what makes you think you can turn them around? As you and I make more posts to this thread, it just serves to bring out more & more insulting responses from these same punks. However, you and I have one distinct advantage. As time moves on some of these kids will grow up and get married and have a couple of kids (whom they would like to protect).... Then one morning they will wake up and find that they are you. Then they will remember that in the Archives of some Forum somewhere is proof of what they said and what they did TODAY.<P>I'd suggest that you do what I do. Whenever I see a post asking for help made by someone with a sig file or I.D. that I find distasteful... I just don't answer their request for help. Even if I know exactly what their problem is, I don't answer them. <P>This is kinda fun to do because every once in a while this person will post another message to the Forum about a week later and he'll be crying in his Kool-Aide because no one answered his request for help.<P>Ok kiddies, take some shots at me..... see if you can insult me before you embarrass yourself.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000024||Cooter||09-04-2001||11:49 PM||||It is a matter of common decency and respect. Some have it and some don't. Most people should have learned to be decent, respect should be earned. Because of some members' views, I have no respect for them and could care less if I offend them, but the members who have common decency, morals and values have earned my respect and hopefully the respect of others too. Hugh and I do not see eye to eye on some issues on the forum, but I respect his views and stand on this issue. I am not easily offended, but I still should not be subjected to the some of the stuff that takes place here. You will say- if you don't like it, don't read it. To that, I will say- I should not have to wade through other people's crap mouth writings just to enjoy the Forum.<P>Wow- Archie and I sort of agree. Is it cold in here or what?<p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||frontal lobe||09-05-2001||12:21 AM||||Here's another opinion, Hugh.  I agree with you that many of the sexual references are offensive.<P>Second opinion:  I am so sick of the "any censorship is bad" mindless mantra being thoughtlessly repeated over and over (intentionally redundant for emphasis).<P>If any of you anti-censorship people would use a brain cell for even one fleeting millisecond, you would realize that we all censor ourselves often, and are GLAD we do.  It's all a matter of where you draw the line.<P>So Hugh is just trying to get a feel of where that line is, and possibly asking some people to consider where to CENSOR THEMSELVES (NOT FORCED), and oh, my, we can't have our freedom of expression challenged like that.  Why the nerve.  I have my rights.  You can't shut me up.<P>Yeah, I know, I know.  You have your rights--to be a selfish, self-centered, boorish, dimwitted, immature, small-minded little retard.<P>Hehe.  Hehe.  I showed them.  I said to sit on my face.  Hehe.  Hehe.<P>Yeah, you showed us real good.||||reg||1
