Z||000032||Voytek||09-05-2001||01:05 PM||||Butter - a lot of crap is being pushed now-a-days in the name of 'tolerance'.  The question of decency is not about tolerance, it's about respect for others (like Cooter said).<P>And no, I don't think it's got to do anything with age either.  Let me give you an example.  In my gym it's usually the 70 year old wrinkled dude, with a 50 lb belly and remains of gray hair on his back that will stand outside the shower with his shrunken privates dangling in front of him,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> while he's drying his back for 20 minutes, facing the change room.  It grosses me out, and I tell ya, most YOUNG guys in the gym have a LOT more decency than the old dudes (nothing against the old dudes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).<P>Going back to this topic, while I do not condone offensive phrases on PFF, I think the best thing anyone can do is ask (or tell) others to be more respectful; censoring others is Cliff's job and not ours.<P>By the same token, I believe that any ladies on PFF can type (no duh) and let us know if they're offended; I don't believe they need a Big Brother to protect them.  The other option is leaving the forum (like several male members have threatened to do).<P>In fact, has anyone noticed that the only people that have ever complained about offensive material on PFF are men?  I have yet to see a complaint from a female.<P>Archie said it right - I won't respond to a punk-a$$ either.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
