Z||000041||Philphine||09-05-2001||07:03 PM||||i don't think the ladies should have to say when something is offencive. who's about the youngest regular poster here? 15 or so? by then they and anyone older should have an idea. <P>that just happened to be the last post i saw so i commented on it. what i really wanted to say is similar though. a lot of people keep talking about their right to say what they want. maybe that's so, but along with that right you should have some...maturity? consideration? i'm not sure what the word is but i don't see it as a negative thing to edit yourself or at least be considerate of your audience. <P>i haven't been on the internet that long but i have seen that for some it brings on a kind of turrets syndrome. anything they're thinking comes right out. i know people like to say they would be the same in person and they're not hiding behind a computer, but along with thinking "i'm not ashamed to meet anyone i've spoke to here no matter what i've said", also consider would those people want to meet you after what they seen you write.  <P>hugh, a few people have decided not to bother with off topic. i find myself having to ignore quite a few threads in this section myself. that may be your only option.<P>sorry, "holier than thou" moment there.||||reg||1
